<title>GERMANY: Deutsche shares surge on H1 results.</title>
<headline>Deutsche shares surge on H1 results.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Germany's largest commercial bank Deutsche Bank AG surged over five percent in early IBIS trade after its first half 1997 figures exceeded analysts' expectations.</p>
<p>By 0638 GMT, Deutsche shares stood at 127.40 marks, up 6.40 marks of 5.29 percent. The overall IBIS DAX was also on record turf, up 2.18 percent at 4,391.45 points.</p>
<p>Deutsche's group net income rose 27.5 percent to 1.5 billion marks in the six months to June 30. Analysts had expected the figure to be around 1.36 billion marks.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
